# Add the FLIGHT INTEGRATOR. With spin killed and the estimate perfect, pure-P control drives
# the initial correction but settles at a steady ~15 deg lean (P fin drops as the error
# shrinks, so it balances the gravity-turn torque at a nonzero angle). An integrator winds up
# the steady fin needed to actually hold vertical (error -> 0). It is safe: the flight code
# resets the rate I-terms while on the rail (rkt.hold_integrators()), so it is zero on the pad
# and only active in flight. Watch the steady TRUE tilt drop toward 0 (mission PASS). If it
# overshoots/oscillates or winds up near apogee, trim I down.
ATC_ANG_RLL_P 12.0
ATC_ANG_PIT_P 12.0
ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.5
ATC_RAT_PIT_P 0.5
ATC_RAT_RLL_I 0.3
ATC_RAT_PIT_I 0.3
ATC_RAT_RLL_D 0.02
ATC_RAT_PIT_D 0.02
